course: dictionary
lesson: 11989
title: Words for running a meeting
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A chairman or chairwoman leads a meeting so that everyone can speak and the meeting runs well. The word chairmanship names that job. Look at the words around it: «Under her chairmanship, the school council planted a new garden.» The phrase «under her chairmanship» tells you who was in charge while the garden was planned.
explain: Chairmanship can mean three things: the job itself, the time someone has the job, and the skill of running a meeting well. Read the sentence again and ask which meaning fits. «The chairmanship lasted three years» is about time, but «Ravi showed great chairmanship» is about skill.
explain: Chair is also a word for a seat, so do not confuse them. In «Please pull up a chair», chair means a seat. In «She has the chairmanship», it means the job of leading. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check: «She has the seat» does not make sense, so the job meaning is right.
fact: A chairmanship is the job of being the chair of a meeting, committee or company.
fact: «Under the chairmanship of» means while someone is in charge of a group.
fact: «Take over the chairmanship» means to start doing the job of chair, often after someone else has left it.
fact: Chairmanship can also mean the skill of running a meeting well, such as letting everyone speak and keeping to time.
fact: Chairmanship is an uncountable noun, so we say «great chairmanship», not «a chairmanships».
exercise: «Under her chairmanship, the school council planted a new garden.» What does chairmanship mean here? | A school trip to the park | *The job of being the chair of the meeting | A kind of wooden seat | A list of things to buy
exercise: «The chairmanship lasted three years.» What does this tell you? | How many people came to the meeting | The rules for playing a game | The name of the room where meetings are held | *How long someone held the job of chair
exercise: «Ravi showed great chairmanship, letting everyone speak and keeping the meeting on time.» What is great chairmanship? | Ignoring the rules to finish early | *Running a meeting well | Sitting at the back and saying nothing | Talking more than anyone else
test: «Her chairmanship of the committee started in May.» What does chairmanship mean? | A type of chair with arms | *The job of being the chair of the committee | Lunch break after the meeting
test: Which word means the skill of running a meeting well? | Fatigue | Absence | Attendance | *Chairmanship
exam: Read «Sam took over the chairmanship of the club when Mr Hale retired.» Which phrase best explains chairmanship here? | A type of tent for camping | A game the club plays on Fridays | Lunch served at the club | *The job of leading the club, which Sam started doing
